    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] It was also the highest mountain in India before 1971 when Sikkim, the state in which Kangchenjunga is located, joined the Republic of India.\n[2] The main peak, Trisul I, was the first peak over 7000 m to have ever been climbed, in 1907.\n[3] It was the first mapped peak in the Karakoram mountain range, hence the designation \"K1\".\n[4] Sunanda Devi (Hindi: सुनन्दा देवी ) previously known as Nanda Devi East is the lower of the two adjacent peaks of the highest mountain in Uttarakhand and second highest mountain in India; Nanda Devi is its higher twin peak.\n\nNotes:\n[bridge] Masherbrum is a peak in the Karakoram range, often compared to other high peaks like Nanda Devi."
